# Implement Authentication & Animated Login Flow

This plan outlines the architecture for introducing a secure user authentication system to Scholarium, ensuring that users can register, log in with a password, and have their goals and progress securely saved to their unique profile.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Reset Needed**: Because we are adding passwords and moving to Django's built-in authentication system, the existing `users_user` table needs to be replaced. For a smooth transition in development, **I will need to reset your local database (drop all tables and remigrate)**. Please let me know if there is any critical data you need to preserve before I do this, or if wiping the development database is okay!

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Django)

#### [MODIFY] `backend/scholarium_project/settings.py`
- Add `rest_framework_simplejwt` for JWT-based authentication.
- Add `AUTH_USER_MODEL = 'users.User'`.
- Configure DRF to use `JWTAuthentication` by default.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/users/models.py`
- Modify the existing custom `User` model to inherit from Django's `AbstractUser`. This automatically adds `username`, `password`, `email`, and secure hashing functionalities.

#### [NEW] `backend/users/serializers.py` & `backend/users/views.py`
- Create `UserSerializer` and `RegisterSerializer`.
- Implement `/api/auth/register/` and use simplejwt's built-in `TokenObtainPairView` for `/api/auth/login/`.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/scholarium_project/urls.py`
- Route `/api/auth/` to the new authentication endpoints.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/agent/views.py`
- Secure all API endpoints (e.g., `create_goal`, `start_session`, `get_progress`) with `@permission_classes([IsAuthenticated])`.
- Refactor the code to use `request.user` to associate goals and sessions with the actively logged-in user, rather than expecting a `user_id` from the frontend.

---

### Frontend (React)

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx`
- Create a global React Context to manage authentication state, store the JWT tokens in `localStorage`, and handle the `login`, `register`, and `logout` actions.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.jsx` & `frontend/src/pages/RegisterPage.jsx`
- Build beautifully designed login and registration screens.
- **Cool Live Animations**: I will use `framer-motion` and vanilla CSS to create a dynamic, live background (e.g., floating glowing orbs, smooth gradient meshes) to give the app a premium, state-of-the-art feel as requested.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/components/ProtectedRoute.jsx`
- A wrapper component that redirects unauthenticated users to `/login`.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/App.jsx`
- Integrate `AuthContext` and `ProtectedRoute`.
- Restructure routing so that the `Dashboard`, `Profile`, and `GraphView` are protected.
- Add a "Logout" button to the Navbar that clears the session and returns the user to the animated Login page.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/services/api.js`
- Update Axios interceptors to automatically attach the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header to all requests.
- Handle 401 Unauthorized errors by automatically logging the user out.

